{
  "_readme": "External route census (audit E16a). The nginx configs are the EXTERNAL boundary: every internet-reachable route exists because a server/location block declares it. The compliance service is deliberately NOT internet-routed (no published port; no public vhost proxies to it). tools/check_route_census.py fails on: a parsed route missing here (UNKNOWN), an entry whose route/action no longer parses (STALE), a forbidden pattern (/v1/admin, /cp/, /internal/, /claims) in a public anonymous/customer location, or a public vhost proxying to the compliance port. Classes: anonymous = unauthenticated public marketing/docs/status/health; customer = api/app/enterprise routes whose auth is enforced at the application (session/JWT/API-key); internal = loopback-only listeners and nginx-`internal` error-page locations (never directly reachable); security-review = staff-gated control plane (admin.apexmail.ee, operator auth at api-server).",
  "forbidden_public_patterns": [
    "/v1/admin",
    "/cp/",
    "/internal/",
    "/claims"
  ],
  "compliance_service_port": 3011,
